{
  "_comment": [
    "Base permission set for unattended overnight worker and reviewer sessions.",
    "The runner copies this to .overnight/worker-settings.json and layers conditional rules",
    "on top (package installs, network access) before passing it to `claude -p --settings`.",
    "",
    "Two rules from the permission docs shape everything here:",
    "  1. Deny beats allow, and a broad deny cannot carry exceptions. So denies are narrow.",
    "  2. Path rules are only consulted for Read(...) and Edit(...). Write(...) and Glob(...)",
    "     are accepted but never checked, so secrets are denied as Read and Edit.",
    "",
    "This is one of two layers. Permission rules match the command text Claude writes and are",
    "explicitly not a boundary around a program: `Bash(git push *)` does not match",
    "`git -C . push` or `sh -c 'git push'`. The guard hook in hooks/hooks.json catches those."
  ],
